Chapter: LengthTuning
  cites Foreword chapter List

 Serpentine and trombone length tuning for matched-length and
 time-domain tuned nets. Generates meander patterns to add length
 to traces that are shorter than their target.

Section: Tuning Target

  TuningMode =
    | TuneSingleLength (Integer)
    | TuneDiffPairSkew (Integer)
    | TuneTimeDomain (Integer)
    | TuneGroupMatch (Text)

  TuningProfile = record {
    tp-name : Text,
    tp-mode : TuningMode,
    tp-min-amplitude : Integer,
    tp-max-amplitude : Integer,
    tp-spacing : Integer,
    tp-corner-style : Integer,
    tp-layer : Integer
  }

Section: Meander Segment

  MeanderDirection =
    | MeanderLeft
    | MeanderRight

  MeanderSegment = record {
    ms-x : Integer,
    ms-y : Integer,
    ms-amplitude : Integer,
    ms-half-period : Integer,
    ms-direction : MeanderDirection,
    ms-width : Integer,
    ms-layer : Integer,
    ms-net : Integer
  }

Section: Tuning Result

  TuningResult = record {
    tr-net-name : Text,
    tr-current-length : Integer,
    tr-target-length : Integer,
    tr-added-length : Integer,
    tr-meanders : List MeanderSegment,
    tr-meander-count : Integer,
    tr-achieved : Integer
  }

  tuning-deficit : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tuning-deficit (current) (target) =
    if target > current then target - current else 0

  tuning-surplus : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tuning-surplus (current) (target) =
    if current > target then current - target else 0

Section: Meander Generation

 Calculate the number of meander periods needed to add a given
 length. Each full period adds approximately 2 * amplitude of
 extra trace length.

  meanders-needed : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  meanders-needed (deficit) (amplitude) =
    if amplitude <= 0 then 0
    else let per-meander = amplitude * 2
    in (deficit + per-meander - 1) / per-meander

  generate-meanders : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> TuningResult
  generate-meanders (start-x) (start-y) (deficit) (amplitude) (spacing) (width) (layer) (net) (max-count) =
    let count = meanders-needed deficit amplitude
    in let actual-count = if count > max-count then max-count else count
    in let added = actual-count * amplitude * 2
    in generate-meanders-loop start-x start-y amplitude spacing width layer net actual-count 0 MeanderLeft []

  generate-meanders-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, MeanderDirection, List MeanderSegment -> TuningResult
  generate-meanders-loop (x) (y) (amplitude) (spacing) (width) (layer) (net) (total) (index) (dir) (acc) =
    if index >= total then TuningResult {
      tr-net-name = "",
      tr-current-length = 0,
      tr-target-length = 0,
      tr-added-length = total * amplitude * 2,
      tr-meanders = acc,
      tr-meander-count = total,
      tr-achieved = 1
    }
    else let seg = MeanderSegment {
      ms-x = x + index * spacing,
      ms-y = y,
      ms-amplitude = amplitude,
      ms-half-period = spacing / 2,
      ms-direction = dir,
      ms-width = width,
      ms-layer = layer,
      ms-net = net
    }
    in let next-dir = when dir
      is MeanderLeft -> MeanderRight
      is MeanderRight -> MeanderLeft
    in generate-meanders-loop x y amplitude spacing width layer net total (index + 1) next-dir (list-push acc seg)

Section: Differential Pair Skew

 For differential pairs, the shorter trace needs meanders to match
 the longer trace. The skew is the length difference.

  diff-pair-skew : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  diff-pair-skew (length-p) (length-n) =
    if length-p > length-n then length-p - length-n
    else length-n - length-p

  diff-pair-needs-tuning : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  diff-pair-needs-tuning (length-p) (length-n) (max-skew) =
    if diff-pair-skew length-p length-n > max-skew then 1 else 0
